3	line	Odd Old Man	Oh, you must have got the wrong end of the stick.
3	line	Odd Old Man	I need some fresh, whole bones to replace ones that have become damaged.
3	line	Player	What?
3	line	Odd Old Man	Err...
3	line	Sack	Mumblemumblemumblemumblemumble. Mumblemumblemumblemumble. Mumble.
3	line	Player	Excuse me...
3	line	Sack	Shhh!
3	line	Player	Sorry...
3	line	Sack	Mumblemumble. Mumblemumblemumble.
3	line	Odd Old Man	Ok, got it.
3	line	Odd Old Man	Ok, here is the thing. While sorting out what bones I do have I managed to lose or damage a few. If you can get me some fresh, unbroken bones to use as replacements then I can get on with things.
3	line	Odd Old Man	That make things clearer?
3	line	Player	Well, it makes some sense I suppose...
3	line	Odd Old Man	Great. If you can get me a bone from a Goblin, a Bear, a Big Frog, a Ram, a Unicorn, a Monkey, a Giant rat and a Giant Bat then I'll be able to move on with the...
3	line	Odd Old Man	Displays...
3	line	Player	So you just want me to bring you these bones and that will be that?
3	line	Odd Old Man	Well, I wouldn't mind you sticking them in a pot and boiling them in vinegar first, if you don't mind.
3	line	Odd Old Man	There is a Wine Merchant in Draynor called Fortunato that sells the stuff you'll need.
3	line	Odd Old Man	You can even use my pot-boiler if you want.
3	line	Player	Why do I need to boil them in vinegar?
3	line	Odd Old Man	It gets them bright and sparking white.
3	line	Odd Old Man	It's an archaeologist thing.
3	line	Odd Old Man	Just put the bone in a pot of vinegar, throw some logs on the fire, put the pot in the holder and light the logs.
3	line	Odd Old Man	It takes a while for the vinegar to evaporate, but the bone will be nice and clean in the end.
3	line	Player	All right, I'll be back later.
3	line	Odd Old Man	Bye!
3	action	end
